From 2619ce75426e92ef65aab54cc2d24ddf1f3251c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:45:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reorder the Learn menu and split Discover why, per Hila's
 suggestions

- Discover why is split in two:
  - How common? (/learn/how-common): the "how often" statistics, up to
    "...not replace the conversation with your doctor about what's next."
  - How can genetic testing help? (/learn/how-testing-helps): everything
    below, ending with cards for its sub-pages.
  Old /learn/discover-why and /learn/how-it-helps addresses redirect.
- Learn menu order: How common?; How can genetic testing help? (sub-pages
  Guide care, Help your family, Support living donor decisions); Signs
  testing may help; How testing works (sub-page Types of tests); Genetic
  counselors; Your rights & choices; APOL1; Understanding your genetic
  test report; Sharing with family; Find a support group; Explore
  research opportunities.
- Sub-pages are indented under their parent in the header and mobile
  menus, and their banner has a link back to the parent page.
- "Uncertain results / VUS" is now labeled "Understanding your genetic
  test report" in menus and cards.
- Getting started cards show the top-level pages only, in the new order.
- Signs testing may help: two sentences linking to the Genetic Risk Check
  and How to get tested.
- FAQ: new "How common is a genetic cause of kidney disease?" question;
  "Why would I get genetic testing?" now points to How can genetic
  testing help?. Search index refreshed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012p2rj8y1uznXf4UStSfSh8
